## 10. Anti-Patterns to Avoid

**DON'T**:
- $match after $lookup (filter before lookup)
- Using `$unwind` without an early `$match` on top-level fields (explodes too many docs)
- Querying without indexes on the fields used in `$match` (collection scans are slow)
- Multiple sequential $lookup stages (denormalize or combine)
- Bare $group without $match (groups entire collection)
- $sort before $limit without index (sorts everything)
- Projecting all fields before $lookup (transfer unnecessary data)
- Ignoring allowDiskUse for large aggregations (100MB memory limit)

**DO**:
- Filter early on top-level fields (smallest dataset before $unwind)
- Use indexed fields in $match, including compound indexes covering array fields
- Project only needed fields
- Use `$reduce` or `$filter` when you don't need to filter on multiple array element fields
- Combine lookups when possible
- Enable allowDiskUse for large aggregations
- Check explain() output before deploying
- Create compound indexes for common query patterns including array fields

