## 7. Using $indexHint with Aggregation Pipelines

Sometimes MongoDB's query planner picks a suboptimal index. You can force index usage with `$indexHint`:

```javascript
db.orders.aggregate([
    {$match: {orderDate: {$gte: ISODate("2024-01-01")}, "items.status": "shipped"}},
    {$indexHint: {orderDate: 1, "items.status": 1}}
])
```

This is especially useful when you have a compound index that covers both the filter and subsequent sorting.

