## 10. Anti-Patterns to Avoid

**DON'T**:
- $match after $lookup (filter before lookup)
- $lookup without index on foreign field
- Using `$unwind` without an immediate `$match` to discard unwanted array elements
- Querying without indexes on filter fields
- Multiple sequential $lookup stages when a single pipeline lookup can suffice
- $sort before $limit without index on sort field
- Ignoring allowDiskUse for large aggregations (100MB memory limit)
- Using `$push` to accumulate full documents in `$group`

**DO**:
- Filter early (smallest dataset possible)
- Use indexed fields in $match
- Project only needed fields before `$lookup`
- Place `$match` immediately after `$unwind` to reduce intermediate document count
- Create compound indexes that cover filters, sort, and projections
- Enable allowDiskUse for large aggregations
- Check explain() output before deploying

