## 10. Anti-Patterns to Avoid

**DON’T**:
- `$match` after `$lookup` on local fields that could have been filtered earlier (but `$match` on looked‑up fields is necessary)
- Using `$filter` inside `$reduce` for large arrays when you need to sort by the aggregated total – `$unwind` + sort is often faster
- Querying without indexes on the main filter and on the array field
- Multiple sequential `$lookup` stages without filtering intermediate results
- Bare `$group` without `$match` (groups entire collection)
- `$sort` before `$limit` without an index (sorts everything)
- Projecting all fields before `$lookup` (transfer unnecessary data)
- Ignoring `allowDiskUse` for large aggregations (100MB memory limit)

**DO**:
- Filter early on local fields (orderDate)
- Use an index on the array field (`items.status`)
- Perform `$unwind` only when necessary; consider `$filter` if you don’t need to sort by aggregated values
- Index the foreign collection for `$lookup`
- Enable `allowDiskUse` for pipelines that explode documents
- Check `explain()` output before deploying
- Create compound indexes for common query patterns

